      "id": "fb-001",
      "question": "What happens when a SIM goes offline?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 40.18,
      "answer": "When a SIM goes offline, several factors can be involved, and the system is designed to address these through various features:\n\n1. **Linking and Accountability**: Each SIM should be visibly linked to a specific tracker, asset, branch, and department to avoid confusion during support calls and speed up troubleshooting.\n\n2. **Data-Spend Summaries**: Finance managers can access daily, weekly, and monthly data-spend summaries by telco, country, product, and customer account to monitor connectivity expenses and prevent unnoticed margin erosion.\n\n3. **Automatic Data Ingestion**: The system aims to ingest SIM data automatically from telco APIs to avoid manual updates and stale records, improving accuracy and operating efficiency.\n\n4. **SIM-Commissioning Steps**: Technical installers follow guided steps that capture ICCID, IMEI, APN, test signal, and first heartbeat to ensure the SIM is installed correctly, reducing avoidable repeat visits.\n\n5. **Roaming Status and Cost Impact**: Cross-border fleet owners can see roaming status by country and estimated cost impact as soon as a unit crosses a border, allowing for early decision-making to avoid shock bills.\n\n6. **Bundle Recommendations**: The system recommends the most suitable roaming or local bundle for the corridor an asset is entering, helping to keep units online at a lower cost.\n\n7. **Bundle Monitoring**: Support engineers can monitor bundle remaining percentages and projected depletion dates for every active SIM, enabling intervention before a unit goes offline to reduce avoidable downtime.\n\n8. **Network and Signal Monitoring**: For wearable and smartphone SIMs, network type, signal strength, and recent connectivity gaps are shown to judge whether staff are truly unreachable or merely inactive.\n\nThese features are part of the documented design and may not all be live on your account. \n\nSource: OLIWA User Stories — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
      "tools_used": [
        "waswa_context",
        "unit_find(all, prefetched)",
        "knowledge_search(SIM goes offline)"
      ],
