    {
      "id": "fb-004",
      "question": "What is IVMS?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 23.39,
      "answer": "IVMS (In-Vehicle Monitoring System) is part of the vehicle telematics solutions offered in the NAVAS ecosystem. It includes features for stable tracking, compliance, and report readiness. The system is configured to track GPS data such as latitude, longitude, speed, and heading, and it monitors connectivity, power status, and ignition/ACC status. It also applies baseline alerts for overspeed, ignition on/off, geofence in/out, and towing if supported, along with baseline reports like daily trips, stops, mileage, and driver behavior summaries if ECO/DSC is enabled.\n\nSource: NAVAS CMS User Manual — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
